{
  "about": "The status document keeps a team whose Orchestrator is only undecided; the recorded Node status dropped a team with no `created`, older than a day, or whose pid had no recorded start. Native keeps it, because an age or a missing `created` never proves a death. The recordings are not rewritten. A row named here is replayed with the kept team's own contribution removed from both the recorded and the actual status document, and counts as diverged only when it is equal after that; see tests/contract-tools/lib-ledger.mjs, scope status-team.",
  "ruling": "b3 §13; b4 §1 (a); b6 §1",
  "id": "team-filter",
  "reason": "Phase B fail-closed team filter (b3 §13); the recorded Node keeps the pre-#403 age rule",
  "paths": [
    "$.teams[?(@.team == T)]: the element's presence and content",
    "$.owners[*].teams: T in the list; an entry left with no team goes with it; the timeline aggregate fields of an entry that named T",
    "$.member_sessions: extra entries, every recorded one still present and in order",
    "$.timeline[*].{visible,tone,live,out,blocked,overdue,stalled,text,short}: the aggregates over all teams, which T's presence changes"
  ],
  "unmasked": "`written`, `written_at`, `expires_at`, `at`, and every other key",
